# No energy/force/stress accuracy metric is reported in a form the schema captures (see Q12).

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Review first: SI Table S3 gives zero-shot raw and reference-aligned energy RMSE/MAE and force RMSE on this data set for 26 pretrained models (for example orb-v3 30.36 raw / 31.27 aligned meV/atom and 197.29 meV/A; mace-mp-0 90.96 / 44.83 and 509.17; chgnet 368.92 / 55.48 and 486.37; m3gnet 109.65 / 52.47 and 601.14). The models are named by Matbench Discovery keys without release or checkpoint, so they were not matched to registry models (the registry separates several MACE-MP-0, CHGNet, M3GNet and SevenNet checkpoints). With the checkpoints pinned this table is directly encodable.
# - The errors of the eight trained models (Fig. 3), the geometry-specific learning curves, the cross-geometry transfer matrices and mixed-geometry fine-tuning (Fig. 4) are figures only; the text gives approximate values only (mixed-geometry MACE force RMSE from about 100 to 70 meV/A).
# - Fine-tuning from a pretrained model is recorded as a string-valued setting; schema 0.1.2 has no relation between a fine-tuned model and its base model. Wall times are in minutes and kept in the hardware string because mlips:trainingDuration is in hours.
# - Elastic, phonon and surface-energy validations and the neck tensile MD are not encoded. The DFT functional was not captured.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
